         "id": "a",
         "prompt": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int_{2}^{4} r(x)\\,dx \\). Show the work that leads to your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "2\\ln 3 - \\frac{3}{2}\\ln\\frac{11}{7}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Factor the denominator and write the decomposition.",
               "latex": "\\frac{x + 9}{(2x + 3)(x - 1)} = \\frac{A}{2x + 3} + \\frac{B}{x - 1}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Clear denominators: x + 9 = A(x - 1) + B(2x + 3). At x = 1, 10 = 5B; at x = -3/2, 15/2 = -5A/2.",
               "latex": "A = -3, \\quad B = 2"
            },
            {
               "text": "The decomposition.",
               "latex": "r(x) = -\\frac{3}{2x + 3} + \\frac{2}{x - 1}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Antidifferentiate each term, dividing by the leading coefficient 2 in the first.",
               "latex": "\\int r(x)\\,dx = -\\frac{3}{2}\\ln|2x + 3| + 2\\ln|x - 1| + C"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate from 2 to 4.",
               "latex": "\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\ln 11 + 2\\ln 3\\right) - \\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\ln 7 + 2\\ln 1\\right) = 2\\ln 3 - \\frac{3}{2}\\ln\\frac{11}{7}"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "a1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99081",
               "skills": [
